\ Tests of bounded ordered month lengths with 4..123 days each.
\ Small cases were independently enumerated; extreme year counts were
\ checked by an independent inclusion/exclusion computation.
\ These tests do not claim a successful CAL compiler execution.

To check bounded month length counts:
  Count month lengths given 12 and 3.
  If the month length work's count result is not "1",
    put "Twelve days in three months has more than one partition." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 13 and 3.
  If the month length work's count result is not "3",
    put "Thirteen days in three months does not have three partitions." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 20 and 3.
  If the month length work's count result is not "45",
    put "Twenty days in three months has the wrong count." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 123 and 1.
  If the month length work's count result is not "1",
    put "A 123-day month was not accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 124 and 1.
  If the month length work's count result is not "0",
    put "An illegal 124-day month was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 128 and 2.
  If the month length work's count result is not "119",
    put "Two months with 128 days have the wrong count." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 246 and 2.
  If the month length work's count result is not "1",
    put "Two maximum-length months should have one partition." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 247 and 2.
  If the month length work's count result is not "0",
    put "Two months cannot hold 247 days." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 252 and 3.
  If the month length work's count result is not "7021",
    put "Three months in a 252-day year have the wrong count." into the check report; exit.

To verify two month lengths given a number and another number:
  Put the chosen month lengths' first into an examined month length record.
  If the examined month length record is nil,
    put "Month length one is missing." into the check report; exit.
  If the examined month length record's days in month is not the number,
    put "Month length one differs from its reference." into the check report; exit.
  Put the examined month length record's next into the examined month length record.
  If the examined month length record is nil,
    put "Month length two is missing." into the check report; exit.
  If the examined month length record's days in month is not the other number,
    put "Month length two differs from its reference." into the check report; exit.
  If the examined month length record's next is not nil,
    put "A two-month partition has an unwanted third month." into the check report; exit.

To check month length lexical ranking:
  Put 128 into the chosen year's year length.
  Put 2 into the selected month count.
  Put "1" into a test month rank wide quantity.
  Select month lengths from the test month rank wide quantity.
  If the month length work's valid selection is not 1,
    put "The first two-month length sequence was rejected." into the check report; exit.
  Verify two month lengths given 5 and 123.
  Put "60" into the test month rank wide quantity.
  Select month lengths from the test month rank wide quantity.
  Verify two month lengths given 64 and 64.
  Put "119" into the test month rank wide quantity.
  Select month lengths from the test month rank wide quantity.
  Verify two month lengths given 123 and 5.
  Put "120" into the test month rank wide quantity.
  Select month lengths from the test month rank wide quantity.
  If the month length work's valid selection is not 0,
    put "An out-of-range month-length rank was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Put "0" into the test month rank wide quantity.
  Select month lengths from the test month rank wide quantity.
  If the month length work's valid selection is not 0,
    put "A zero month-length rank was accepted." into the check report; exit.

\ This is expensive because it evaluates inclusion/exclusion for a
\ 47-month year with 4244 days. It is an optional slow check.
To check a large month length count:
  Count month lengths given 252 and 47.
  If the month length work's count result is not "22747362824110665179416185383175",
    put "A 252-day 47-month count lost big-number precision." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 4244 and 47.
  If the month length work's count result is not "32170173581666034502316982845062598233361029508388020389719545988110540721085603322536940",
    put "The 4244-day 47-month count lost big-number precision." into the check report; exit.
  Count month lengths given 5778 and 47.
  If the month length work's count result is not "18424",
    put "The longest year has the wrong maximal month-count compositions." into the check report; exit.
